# `module::Field::Result`

What pricing returns: the prices, the Greeks, and (for the FFT engine) the strike grid. It is the type `Field::price` returns, and the one a [`Chord::Result`](../chord/Result.md) holds for each asset; it is declared by the pricer layer, which the engines also return it from, and `Field::Result` is its name on a field.

`price` has one entry per option in the strip. `greeks` is a [`Greeks`](Greeks.md) whose members are defined only under `Risk::All`. `strike_grid` is defined only when the FFT engine was asked to return its grid (`Fft::return_grid`). In that case `price` is no longer one entry per option: it holds the transform's price at **every** strike of the grid (16384 entries by default), and `strike_grid` holds those strikes, from which any strike in the range can be read.

## Fields

### `price`

`pluss::Series`, default `undefined`.

One price per option.

### `greeks`

`pricer::Greeks`, default `{}`.

The Greeks; defined only under `Risk::All`.

### `strike_grid`

`pluss::Series`, default `undefined`.

The strikes of the FFT grid when `return_grid` was set; undefined otherwise.

## Guidance

Returned by `Field::price` and the engines' `price`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

The grid. With `return_grid` the FFT engine returns its price at every strike of the transform, with the strikes beside it; without it, one price for the one option.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(0));
  mod::Field field{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(fin::pricing::Call, 100.0, 1.0),
                   .market = fin::market::make(100.0, 0.02, 0.0),
                   .model = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::Heston, {1.5, 0.04, 0.3, -0.7, 0.04}),
                   .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Fft, .risk = mod::Risk::PriceOnly}};

  const auto single = field.price();
  field.controls.fft.return_grid = true;
  const auto grid = field.price();
  out.writeln("single: price", single.price.sizes(), " grid defined", single.strike_grid.defined());
  out.writeln("grid  : price", grid.price.sizes(), " strike_grid", grid.strike_grid.sizes());
}
```

### Example 2

Prices of a strip with Greeks.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  mod::Field field{.instrument = {.type = fin::pricing::Call, .strike = pluss::series::linspace(80.0, 120.0, 5, pluss::ScalarType::Float64), .maturity = pluss::make_series({1.0})},
                   .market = {.spot = pluss::make_series({100.0}), .rate = pluss::make_series({0.05}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({0.0})},
                   .model = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::BlackScholes, {0.2}),
                   .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Analytic, .risk = mod::Risk::All}};

  const auto r = field.price();
  out.writeln("price :", r.price.items<double>());
  out.writeln("delta :", r.greeks.delta.items<double>());
}
```

### Example 3

Without the grid request the grid is undefined.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  mod::Field field{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(fin::pricing::Call, 100.0, 1.0),
                   .market = fin::market::make(100.0, 0.02, 0.0),
                   .model = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::Heston, {1.5, 0.04, 0.3, -0.7, 0.04}),
                   .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Cos, .risk = mod::Risk::PriceOnly}};

  const auto r = field.price();
  out.writeln("strike_grid defined:", r.strike_grid.defined());
}
```

